{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Google Matrix.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Google Matrix.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"google matrix google matrix","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Google Matrix.md","fileName":"Google Matrix.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Google Matrix","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 00:13\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[PageRank and Link Analysis]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["PageRank and Link Analysis","PageRank","Dangling Node","PageRank Teleportation","PageRank Vector","algorithms.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Google Matrix.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Google Matrix.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"google matrix google matrix","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Google Matrix.md","fileName":"Google Matrix.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Google Matrix","heading":"Google Matrix","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The Google matrix is the transition matrix used by the complete [[PageRank]] algorithm. It begins with the web's normalized link structure, repairs rows associated with [[Dangling Node|dangling nodes]], and mixes link-following with [[PageRank Teleportation]].\n\nEvery possible move receives a nonzero probability, so repeated multiplication avoids trapped rank and converges to a stable [[PageRank Vector]]. The matrix need not be stored densely; its result can be computed from the sparse hyperlink structure and the teleportation adjustment.","tags":["baby"],"links":["PageRank and Link Analysis","PageRank","Dangling Node","PageRank Teleportation","PageRank Vector","algorithms.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Google Matrix.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Google Matrix.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__",